// Daisy Seed platform description for Renode.
//
// Layered on top of Renode's stock stm32h743 platform (Cortex-M7, GPIO,
// QUADSPI, SDRAM, EXTI, ...). We specialise it for the Daisy Seed:
//
//   1. Internal flash shrunk to 128 KiB (H750 has one 128 KiB sector,
//      not the 1 MiB of H743). Bootloader is linked for this smaller region.
//   2. SDRAM shrunk to 64 MiB (per libDaisy: SDRAM_SIZE = 0x0400_0000).
//      Renode's default was 256 MiB; shrinking it makes OOB accesses fault.
//   3. IS25LP064A QSPI NOR chip model attached to the QUADSPI controller.
//   4. On-board user LED wired to PC7.
//
// Firmware-visible memory map:
//   0x0800_0000..0x0801_FFFF   internal flash (128 KiB)
//   0x1FF0_0000..0x1FF1_FFFF   system flash (ROM DFU, readonly)
//   0x2000_0000..0x2001_FFFF   DTCM SRAM (128 KiB)
//   0x2400_0000..0x2407_FFFF   AXI SRAM (512 KiB)
//   0x3000_0000..0x3004_7FFF   SRAM1+2+3 in D2 (288 KiB)
//   0x3800_0000..0x3800_FFFF   SRAM4 in D3 (64 KiB)
//   0x3880_0000..0x3880_0FFF   Backup SRAM (4 KiB, battery-backed on hw)
//   0x9000_0000..0x907F_FFFF   QSPI XIP window (8 MiB)
//   0xC000_0000..0xC3FF_FFFF   FMC SDRAM (64 MiB)

using "platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl"

flashBank1:
    size: 0x20000

sdramBank1:
    size: 0x4000000

// User LED — two lines are required (verified against
// platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl in the Renode 1.16 install):
//   1) declare the LED peripheral attached to a GPIO port + pin,
//   2) route the GPIO pin's output signal to the LED's input.
userLed: Miscellaneous.LED @ gpioPortC 7

gpioPortC:
    7 -> userLed@0

// DWT (Data Watchpoint and Trace) — Cortex-M debug peripheral. Renode's
// stock stm32h743.repl omits it; our bootloader enables DWT.CYCCNT and
// polls the cycle counter for alive-blink and boot-window timing. Set
// frequency to match our 400 MHz sysclk so `cortex_m::asm::delay` cycle
// counts translate to the same wall-clock durations as on real hardware
// (approximately — Renode's virtual clock has jitter that our LED
// assertions already tolerate).
dwt: Miscellaneous.DWT @ sysbus 0xE0001000
    frequency: 400000000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// IS25LP064A QSPI NOR flash backing store.
//
// Baseline (hybrid) approach: `Memory.MappedMemory` at 0x9000_0000
// so the CPU translator can XIP-execute (Renode's tcg requires a
// real memory region for instruction fetches — peripheral-backed
// regions can be made to work with a vendored renode-infrastructure,
// see vendor/renode-infrastructure/PATCH.md). The QUADSPI controller
// drives the SPI protocol against the flash chip on every CCR write
// that enters memory-mapped mode, blitting the protocol-produced
// bytes back into MappedMemory via IS25LP064A_Fixed.DirectWrite —
// so a broken CCR corrupts the vector table and CPU faults, the same
// failure mode real silicon exhibits.
//
// The `qspiFlash: SPI.IS25LP064A_Fixed @ qspi { underlyingMemory: ... }`
// binding is declared in `stubs.robot` (paths need `${CURDIR}`
// interpolation).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

// XIP-fidelity (Approach B): the QSPI controller now serves the 0x9000_0000
// window itself (BusMultiRegistration "xip", declared in stubs.robot) and drives
// the SPI protocol on every CPU fetch. This MappedMemory is only the flash chip's
// private backing store (IS25LP064A_Fixed.underlyingMemory); it lives off the
// firmware map at 0xA000_0000 so the CPU only ever reaches it *through* the
// controller, never directly.
qspiFlashBacking: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0xA0000000
    size: 0x800000

// STM32H7 peripheral stubs (PWR/RCC/FLASH/SYSCFG) are NOT declared here
// because their `filename:` paths must be absolute — Renode resolves
// them relative to its own install directory, not the .repl file.
// Each Robot test adds them via `LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString`
// with interpolated `${CURDIR}` paths after loading this base platform.
// See boot_blink.robot / app_standalone.robot for the pattern and
// peripherals/NOTICE.md for the rationale.
